WEBVTT

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:06.060
Kuro!

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.120
Look, I didn't mean any harm.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.630
Are you actually that shocked?

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.720
Kinda.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.150
I mean, when I heard you had amnesia,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.990
I believed it! I even cried over it!

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.560
But why? Why did you lie to me?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.780
I got played again.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.250
I'll never be able to trust you after this.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.090
Glance...

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.420
What's with those eyes?

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.500
You laughed at me for 
getting tricked by you.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.170
I-I'm not laughing! You're making 
this out to be worse than it is!

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.170
Why did you lie to me, then?

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.140
Why do I need to tell you? Figure it out!

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.080
I'm not gonna know unless you tell me!

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.380
If there's something you 
wanna say, say it out loud!

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.260
What, you need everything spelled 
out for you verbally? Are you dumb?

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.430
So black-hearted.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.490
What? Wait a minute.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.730
I think you just said something 
you're never supposed to.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.290
<b>Taboo: Any Insult That Uses "Black"</b>

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.650
The Black Ships are here.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.420
<i>Open up
 your country</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.130
Open up your country.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.530
Hey! That's a declaration of war!

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.410
You know that, right?!

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.630
Clover Z!

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.090
Oh? I guess you're all prepared 
for consequences, huh?

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.930
It's your own fault!

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.820
If you apologize right now, I'll hear 
out your reason for lying to me!

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.860
I can't say yet if I'll forgive you, though.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.530
Well, if you want to beg 
for forgiveness from me,

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:33.860
I'm willing to hear you out, too.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.530
Why should I beg for forgiveness?!
<i>You</i> tricked <i>me</i>!

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.200
Because you won't take a hint!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.930
And because you said stuff that's taboo!

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.270
That's why!

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.870
You're not making sense, 
you black-hearted monster!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.250
You said it again!

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.450
Black! Black! Heart! Heart! 
Black! Black! Heart!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.800
You jerk!

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.370
What the hell? I'm not 
the one to blame here...

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:16.900
Osamake: Romcom Where
The Childhood Friend Won't Lose

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.160
I shouldn't have said that!

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.180
What do I do now? Kuro was seriously mad!

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.610
She'll probably try to get back at me!

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:42.250
It was my fault.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:46.280
She'd totally do it! Should I beg for 
forgiveness before it's too late?!

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:51.250
Kuroha-san lied to try to repair 
her relationship with you.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.240
In other words, she did 
it because she likes you.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.470
If that's true, why did she reject you?

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.050
She's just gonna shoot you down again.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.300
That's one convincing devil!

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.480
The angel never stood a chance!

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.710
What the heck is Kuro thinking?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:12.020
If she'd just be up front and apologize,
I'd forgive her.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:13.890
Stupid Haru!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.590
Why doesn't he get it?

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.070
At this rate...

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.210
No!

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:25.240
But if I talk to him now, 
we'll just end up fighting.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.260
Isn't there anyone who can arbitrate for us?

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.900
Um, Kuro-neesan?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.750
<i>What did you just say?</i>

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:42.170
<i>Shirokusa-chan, you lost a lot 
of ground in this whole thing.</i>

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.590
<i>Shida-san's relationship with 
Maru-kun is back to where it was</i>

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.520
<i>before the confession festival, right?</i>

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.790
<i>Your dream came true, 
but it set your romance back.</i>

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.220
It's unusual for you to call. What's up?

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.540
<i>There's something I want to ask you.</i>

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.590
<i>Are you still working with Shida-san?</i>

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.530
Nah.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.950
Once we finished shooting 
the commercial, our working

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.000
<i>relationship was over.</i>

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.940
So can I consider you a neutral party now?

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.040
<i>Nope.</i>

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.130
I'm with...

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.090
whichever side is more interesting.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.480
<i>And? What did you want?</i>

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.300
<i>I have a proposal.</i>

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.670
Oh?

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.020
<i>If he weren't Su-chan's friend, 
I wouldn't even want to talk to him.</i>

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.880
<i>But if I want to win,</i>

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.820
<i>I can't be picky about my methods.</i>

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.340
Everyone's here, right?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:49.240
Celebrate! Maria-chan has 
\h\h\h\h\h\hofficially joined the Ultramarine Alliance!

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.940
First of all, Maria-chan, welcome 
to Hozumino High School.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.840
You're transferring next week, right?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.230
Yes. I look forward to 
being with all of you.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:55.200
On that note, I'd like to go 
over the structure and system

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.950
of the Ultramarine Alliance again.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:10.720
• Rights and obligations of the members 
1) Official members → Positions {column under this is incomplete and will be seen later} 
☆Right to submit proposals 
The same proposal may only be presented once per month 
☆Right to vote 
One vote per person, majority wins 
Votes must be anonymous 
☆Right to veto 
Only once per month (must sign name) 
*Since this is the first meeting, we'll try to avoid this 
☆Obligation to participate in projects 
Any who do not participate may not vote 
2) Unofficial members 
☆Can only participate in projects 
(The only unofficial member currently is Asagi Rena)

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:00.590
First, I'll explain official membership 
and unofficial membership.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:05.380
Official members have the right to 
propose projects, vote on them, and veto them.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.760
They must participate in 
a project they voted on,

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.710
and if they can't participate, 
they can't vote on it in the first place.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.970
<b>The Alliance's Number 2 

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.970
<b>The Alliance's Brains 

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.970
<b>The Alliance's Golden Rookie

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.980
But if even one member uses their 
right to veto, the plan is dropped.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:21.610
<b>The Alliance's Ringleader 

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:21.610
<b>The Alliance's Non-Returner 

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:20.150
And those who lack these rights but participate
 in projects are called unofficial members.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.620
Rena's the only one right now.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.610
<b>Unofficial Member 

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.030
I wasn't looking.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.410
Also, the addition of new members

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.590
will depend on the official members' votes.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:35.540
Huh? Should we really be that choosy?

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.790
About 80% of the people looking 
to join us right now are guys.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.770
I get it! So we need that right to veto!

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.540
I'm glad you gave us that! 
Good thinking, Tetsuhiko!

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.920
That means 20% are girls, then.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.380
Are they after Tetsuhiko?

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.780
He does have fans in other schools.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.110
I do wish that was all they were.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:01.030
Anyway, the point is, we'll deliberate 
carefully when adding new members.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:04.570
And now, we'll begin our 
first planning meeting.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:05.900
Our first proposal is...

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:27.920
First Ultramarine Alliance Planning Meeting 
Proposed by: Kai Tetsuhiko (placed 1st in the vote for projects the Alliance wants to do) 
Plan: Have the 3 female official members shoot a music video 
(Swimsuits encouraged!)

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.620
This!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.760
Swimsuits encouraged?! It's October, dude!

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.990
Actually, I have connections in Okinawa.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.770
It's still warm there, and we can swim.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:16.840
What about money?

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.860
We have the profit from winning 
the commercial contest.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.950
Our goal is to get the 
Ultramarine Alliance's name out there,

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:25.790
so even if the singing and dancing sucks, 
it's fine as long as it draws attention.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.920
I have a song and choreography ready, too.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.170
I always thought you were a genius.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.800
I knew it all along, personally.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:41.130
Why are you two enjoying this so much?!

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.440
You want us in swimsuits?! Unbelievable!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.400
Both of you, get down on your 
knees right where you are!

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:49.580
Please! Girls in swimsuits 
are every man's dream!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.230
Huh?!

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.180
Haru, you lecher! Pervert! Pervert! Pervert!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.200
<b><i>Pervert!</i></b>

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.200
<b><i>Pervert!</i></b>

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.200
<b><i>Pervert!!</i></b>

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.670
To be honest, I'm opposed to this, too.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.550
I mean, asking us to wear swimsuits...

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.780
But you're fine with singing and dancing?

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.670
Well, if we do that, I'm fairly 
confident that I can pull it off.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.910
What about you?

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:08.110
Of course I can't. I'm a complete novice.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:10.060
You're opposed to this, then?

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:10.670
Yes.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:14.760
Then we can probably vote it down 
without having to use a veto.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:19.200
It's best if we can save 
that for another time.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.070
No.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.890
Sorry, but I don't trust 
either of you that much.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:27.590
You complain now, but you might 
decide you're all for it later.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:31.550
And if you do that, this plan 
will have a chance at passing.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:32.270
So...

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:34.670
I demand a revision to this plan.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.750
Remove the part about swimsuits.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.140
If you don't, I'll use my right to veto.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.060
This is the smallest concession I can make.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.740
It's your own fault for proposing a plan

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.410
that you knew someone would 
likely use their veto on.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.630
I don't want to waste my right to veto.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.640
Oh, fine.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:51.710
Swimsuits encouraged!

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:51.760
Swimsuits encouraged!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:51.840
Swimsuits encouraged!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:51.880
Swimsuits encouraged!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:51.920
Swimsuits encouraged!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:52.590
Swimsuits encouraged!

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.910
Happy now?

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:58.000
This still doesn't change the fact 
that we're being put on display.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.040
It's sounding like this is 
going to be voted down.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:00.180
<b>Vote Box</b>

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:00.310
<b>Vote Box</b>

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:00.430
<b>Vote Box</b>

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.020
<b>Vote Box</b>

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.880
There you go. The plan passed.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.810
Yes

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.810
No

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:04.820
Who voted yes?!

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.010
That's what I'd like to ask.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:11.270
You didn't kick up all that fuss only to 
vote in favor behind our backs, did you?

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:13.100
What?! Why would I?

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:16.030
Well, you're fighting with 
Su-chan right now, aren't you?

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.630
It makes sense that you'd want 
a chance to reconcile with him.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.920
That's a very convincing opinion.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.520
N-No! I didn't—

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.630
Okay, okay, no asking how others voted.

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:28.550
Then what's the point of voting anonymously?

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.880
Okinawa 
2 nights, 3 days

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:31.880
On that note,

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.510
Okinawa 
2 nights, 3 days

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:35.330
we'll be staying in Okinawa for two nights 
and three days, starting this Saturday.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.580
What? It's already Wednesday!

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:41.040
Well, it's October. If we're gonna 
go, we want a three-day weekend.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.750
That means this weekend is the best time.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.610
Hang on. I can't go this weekend.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:46.970
My parents are away on business.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.740
If I leave, my little sisters 
will be home alone.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.160
Then bring them along.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:53.890
We'll call them unofficial members.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:54.570
Huh?!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.420
Frankly, I wanted to bring some helpers.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.680
Oh, we'll cover their travel 
expenses, of course.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:02.460
It would definitely be better than 
getting people we don't know to help.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.930
But Midori has a mock exam on Saturday,
 and Aoi has her club...

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:09.670
Then how about we have the Shida 
sisters join us on Sunday?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.610
And we'll shoot on Monday.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.240
You can't just postpone it?

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.400
We won't get another three-day 
weekend for a while.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.150
And we don't know if it'll 
still be sunny in November.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.270
Then can't we just film somewhere closer?

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.590
It doesn't <i>have</i> to be in Okinawa.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:25.700
Part of my goal is to make 
some summer memories.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.240
We formed this club late in the year,

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:30.350
so we didn't get to make 
any summer memories.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.620
The summer of our second year is our last 
summer before we start studying for exams.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:37.510
That means this is our last 
chance to make up for that.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:38.870
That's just...

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.300
Anyone else have a conflict?

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.220
I'll make it work through sheer willpower!

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.620
It's fine with me.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.570
Me, too.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:50.310
Hey, if you want helpers, what about Meiko?

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:53.450
If I ask her, I think she'll 
say she wants to go.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:55.800
Go ahead and ask.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:59.320
All right...

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.690
No, it's okay. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.450
I never thought she'd say no.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:09.830
Remember, it's not good to recommend 
someone if you didn't check with them first.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:11.730
What about my sisters?

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.460
That was because you can't leave 
them at home on their own.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.930
If they say they don't want to go,
 you won't be participating.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:19.410
Got it.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.850
Man, Okinawa, huh?

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.770
I didn't think I'd get to go to the beach.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.640
I had totally given up on that!

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.510
Haru, it's fine to be excited,

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.450
but don't you have midterms next week?

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.920
You did horribly on your last exams, too.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.180
Won't you be in trouble if 
you don't turn it around?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:41.390
Tetsuhiko-kun, you don't mind if 
this trip doubles as a study camp

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.450
for those of us with bad grades, do you?

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.020
I suppose not.

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:48.140
I don't want the club to be blamed 
for anyone getting a failing grade.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.730
Wait, I'm the only one here with bad grades!

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.500
So the study camp's just for me?!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.320
Midori's studying for entrance exams,
 so she'll be there, too.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.590
That just leaves...

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.040
Momo-san, have you taken your transfer exam?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.810
No, I forced my way in with 
money and influence. Why?

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:06.810
Momo! A little sister type 
shouldn't say that!

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:09.990
That doesn't make it better!

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:13.900
Well, whatever... So what were your 
grades like at your previous school?

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.710
I don't think that's something 
I should openly discuss.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.370
What about you?

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.700
There are bad grades and there are 
worse grades. How bad are yours?

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.120
Tee-hee!

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.130
Ow!

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.290
What the hell?!

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.700
So I guess you'll be at the study camp, too.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:26.790
I dunno. You pissed me off.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:31.660
Well, before now, I was grateful to have the 
bare minimum in both grades and attendance.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.500
Why would that piss you off?!

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:29.970
What if a girl smiled at you?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:30.790
She'd be cute!

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.000
And if a guy did it?

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.600
Anyway, Tetsuhiko-san...

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.000
It's be gross!

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.600
Do we know where we'll be staying?

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.650
No worries.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:41.870
Kachi's dad is letting us use 
his villa and private beach.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.480
Oh, so that's it.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.610
You and Tetsuhiko-kun are working together.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.340
What? Me, working with Kai-kun?

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:53.880
You know that would never happen.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.360
You had him add the swimsuit thing 
and then got him to remove it

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.230
to force the proposal through?

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.770
You two planned all of this?!

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:03.260
That was brilliant, Shirokusa-san.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.510
Kuro, why all the animosity toward Shiro?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.720
What?! So you believe Kachi-san?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:12.780
I mean, it doesn't even make sense 
that this was all Shiro's plan.

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:15.750
Why don't you ever believe me?!

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:18.140
Okay, do you believe me, then?

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:22.350
If you did, wouldn't you tell me 
everything and not hide it all?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.950
Osamake: Romcom Where
The Childhood Friend Won't Lose

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.950
<b>\hEpisode 7 
I Know! Let's Go to Okinawa!</b>

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.950
<b>So awkward,
she put down
the camera</b>

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.950
<b>Drop</b>

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:34.890
Huh? Aoi-chan?

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:35.620
Yes.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:40.220
Kuro-neesan couldn't come today, 
so I came in her place.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.990
Oh, okay. Thanks for that.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.760
Not at all. Leave the cleaning to me.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.420
There's one more kitty now...

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:54.340
Kitty says, "Meow, meow"... 
Try to be a kitty...

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:00.530
U-Um, Haru-niisan... were you... listening?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.480
Nah, don't worry. I didn't hear a thing.

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:08.610
U-Um, Haru-niisan...

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:12.750
"Don't worry" is what you would 
say if you heard it, isn't it?

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:16.150
If you hadn't, you'd say, 
"Did you say something?"

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:18.080
or something like that, wouldn't you?

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.210
Oh...

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.100
S'all good!

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.250
You're mean, Haru-niisan!

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.970
Hey, I'm sorry, okay?

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:28.090
I didn't mean to tease you.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.000
It's okay, then.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.310
It was my own fault for singing out loud.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.630
It's so easy to make up with you, Aoi-chan.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:37.690
Huh?

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:40.260
Oh, uh... I just said you're 
a really nice girl.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.430
Please. You'll make me blush.

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.870
I'll be done with this soon. 
Then we can have dinner.

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:46.610
Okay.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.450
I can't wait to eat your curry.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:52.570
Let's eat.

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:59.490
This is it! This is the 
flavor! It's so relaxing!

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:02.570
You always say stuff to lift me up.

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:04.530
Well, that's how I really feel.

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:07.250
You put honey in it just for me, don't you?

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.770
That makes me really happy.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.750
By the way, Haru-niisan...

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.330
You and Kuro-neesan had a fight, didn't you?

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:24.010
She was acting funny, 
so I thought you must have.

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:26.960
Uh, it's probably not something 
I should tell you—

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.630
No, please tell me about it.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:34.050
I respect both of you, 
so I want to help somehow!

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.780
I'm a little embarrassed, 
since it involves love and stuff.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.820
I'll still listen, if you don't mind.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.580
I see. So that's what happened.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:48.140
So... what do you think?

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:50.400
Which one of us is in the wrong here?

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:52.830
Let me see...

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.710
The first response that comes to me is,

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.970
Even
a dog
will
stay

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.970
"Even a dog will stay out 
of a lovers' quarrel."

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.970
out of
a lovers'
quarrel

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:06.820
Your fight is so overflowing with the power 
of love that I feel full just hearing about it.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.130
It just makes me feel exhausted.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:09.940
That's your opinion?!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:12.890
If I were to be honest, 
I think you're both at fault.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:14.520
In fact, I don't even care.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:18.360
Like, shouldn't you just make 
up and start dating already?

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.070
Hang on! Kuro and I are fighting for real!

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.170
My opinion takes that into consideration.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.160
Let me add some more detail here!

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.280
Kuro won't tell me how she really feels.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:32.070
Which means she lied because there's 
something she wants to hide, right?

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:34.520
You're just full of distrust, aren't you?

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:36.140
Well, so is Kuro.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.440
She lied because she didn't trust me.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:44.540
Not everyone can be as 
emotionally open as you are.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:45.090
Huh?

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:48.350
I think you're the kind 
of person who can't lie.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:53.170
But it's difficult for others to be 
like that on the same level as you.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.070
Are you saying I'm the one at fault?

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:58.320
No, I think Kuro-neesan is the one to blame.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.890
But I can understand all 
too well how she feels.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:06.690
So I just wish you would do your best 
to accept her with an open mind.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.760
Kuro-neesan is focusing on the results,

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:12.610
while you're focusing on 
the method and process.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:15.200
I think maybe you're just 
out of sync in that way.

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:17.760
Haru-niisan...

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.970
Do you love Kuro-neesan?

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:23.440
Yeah... but...

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.390
You've found someone else 
that you love more?

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:26.690
Huh?

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.560
I... don't know.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.030
When it comes to love,

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:39.020
I think choosing someone you're 
not fully committed to

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:41.790
will only lead to trouble.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.230
I get that.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.990
Someone I know is the worst example of it.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:49.730
You're going to Okinawa soon, right?

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.970
Oh, are you and your other 
sisters coming, too?

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:54.180
Yes, we'll be there starting 
on the second day.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:58.840
But I think you should be wary of the 
magic of travel while we're there.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.420
Huh? What does that mean?

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:05.030
The moment a boy and girl who had 
nothing between them go on a trip...

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:08.060
Oh! You mean how they get 
excited and end up together?

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:08.650
Yes.

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:10.960
Since you're fighting with Kuro-neesan now,

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.890
if that were to happen, 
I think you'd regret it later.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:16.710
This doesn't sound like your usual advice...

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:18.880
I'm sorry if what I say seems strange.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.860
Nah, thank you, really. 
I'll keep it in mind.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:26.550
Everyone in the Ultramarine 
Alliance is attractive, you know?

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.360
So please...

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.620
Be very careful, okay?

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.620
You're saying... if one of them uses sex 
appeal on me, I'll fall right for it?

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.130
I wouldn't have gone <i>that</i> far.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:38.850
But...

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.160
...I do think that.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.220
<b>Nobody trusts me...</b>

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:50.020
While I was looking into you,

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:54.160
I started looking into Asagi Rena-kun, too.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.570
You know why, don't you?

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.870
Rena doesn't know I'm her 
brother from another mother.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.320
Don't you dare tell her.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.380
So you did know.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:05.070
Of course, I'll keep my word.

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:07.820
If there's anything you want 
of me, I'll do what I can.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:11.470
What's up?

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.290
<i>Today's meeting went just as planned.</i>

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.690
<i>I thought I should thank you.</i>

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.590
You don't need to thank me.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:21.390
But I can look forward to something 
interesting happening, right?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.340
<i>Of course.</i>

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.950
<i>All you need to worry 
about is not interfering.</i>

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:28.110
I would like to know what 
your goal is, though. Well?

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.790
I always have just one goal:

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.310
to get Su-chan to confess 
his love to me. That's it.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.570
Come on, that's gonna be kind of tough.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:36.800
<i>Oh, shut up!</i>

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.060
<i>I'm Su-chan's first love! Do you get that?!</i>

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:43.310
<i>You only have one first love 
in your life! It's special!</i>

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:45.270
<i>So there's nothing tough about it!</i>

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:48.080
I've already perfected the plan 
that I recruited your help for

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:53.010
to win Su-chan over on the day when 
that little homewrecker isn't there.

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:55.920
All you need to do is sit back 
and watch my counterattack.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.070
<i>Understand?</i>

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.920
Yeah, yeah. I understand, madam.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.880
I'll watch and see what you've got.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:07.900
<i>If Sueharu gets a girlfriend, 
the Ultramarine Alliance will blow apart.</i>

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:10.810
<i>So keeping things balanced 
would be ideal for me.</i>

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:14.100
<i>But if Kachi doesn't play her cards right,</i>

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.360
<i>Shida-chan will be a hurdle 
she can never get over.</i>

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.970
<i>And it'll be interesting to see 
what Maria-chan does, too.</i>

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:22.160
<i>I should be excited to 
see how this turns out.</i>

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:31.080
It's summer!

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:35.590
We'll buy food for all three days here.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:39.400
Sorry to make you drive us, as well, Eri-san.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:42.170
My father was supposed to be here...

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:46.460
Oh, it's fine. I was lucky all 
my expenses were covered.

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:49.140
I'm glad to hear you say that.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:55.390
She's really got it together, huh?

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:58.250
I bet she wouldn't call her 
sister on a work night,

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:01.270
and say she can't sleep without 
talking to her, like someone I know.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:02.640
Hey! Onee-chan!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.880
Why did you have to say that?!

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.970
You're ruining my image!

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.810
Oh, what's the problem?

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:11.630
Hey, Sueharu-kun...

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.690
Be honest. Shirokusa-chan's your
 type, isn't she?

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:16.500
Uh... er... no comment.

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:19.170
What about Kuroha-chan? You still love her?

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.370
Where's all this coming from?

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.330
Maria's cute, isn't she?

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.010
Sh-She is, yes.

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:25.670
You won't make her cry, right?

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:30.430
<b>THUMP THUMP THUMP THUMP THUMP</b>

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:28.240
Onee-chan, what's going on?

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:30.430
Hmm? Nothing!

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Seafood</b>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Tempura</b>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Restaurant</b>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Restaurant</b>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Gifts</b>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Seaside Station</b>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.430
<b>Welcome!</b>

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:40.570
<b>Local Specialties</b>

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.830
What meals should we plan to make?

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:38.380
I can make simple Japanese, 
Western, or Chinese dishes.

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.050
Is there anything you'd like?

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:43.930
Wait a minute! You're an
 actress, aren't you?

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:46.210
I thought most actresses couldn't cook.

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:49.420
What? Cooking is easy, though.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:54.100
Wait, is this because your cooking 
skills are dismal, Shirokusa-san?

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:55.470
N-Not at all!

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:57.360
That's not true in the slightest!

00:21:57.630 --> 00:21:58.820
Oh?

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:00.550
I see.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.720
What's with you two?

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:04.060
We never get to travel like this—

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:04.920
Shirokusa-san...

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.920
Yes, the only answer is...

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:08.910
...a cooking contest!
